# NgRx Effects Conventions

## Effect class structure

- **Creating a new effects file?** Filter and dispatch creator-based actions, as below, even when sibling effects files use class-based actions. The one exception is a new effects file that consumes an existing class-based actions file: it uses that file's classes.
- **Adding to an existing file?** Match that file. A file that uses `new WidgetDetailActions.LoadWidgetDetailSuccess(widget)` and string constants keeps them. Do not mix styles within a file or migrate it incidentally.

Inject `Actions`, `Store` and services with `inject()`, not constructor injection. Declare every effect with `createEffect()`.

```typescript
import { inject, Injectable } from '@angular/core';

import { Actions, createEffect, ofType } from '@ngrx/effects';
import { Action, Store } from '@ngrx/store';
import { Observable, of } from 'rxjs';
import { catchError, map, switchMap } from 'rxjs/operators';

import { WidgetApiService } from '@myorg/data';

import * as fromReducer from '../reducers';
import { WidgetActions } from '../actions';

@Injectable()
export class WidgetEffects {
  private actions$ = inject(Actions);
  private store = inject<Store<fromReducer.State>>(Store);
  private widgetApiService = inject(WidgetApiService);

  loadWidget$: Observable<Action> = createEffect(() =>
    this.actions$.pipe(
      ofType(WidgetActions.loadWidget),
      switchMap(({ widgetId }) =>
        this.widgetApiService.getWidget(widgetId).pipe(
          map((widget) => WidgetActions.loadWidgetSuccess({ widget })),
          catchError(() => of(WidgetActions.loadWidgetError()))
        )
      )
    )
  );
}
```

## API calls — through API services only

All HTTP/API calls go through the domain API services of rule `client-data-api-service`, imported through their library alias. Never use raw `HttpClient` in effects. Never use deep relative paths into the libs folder.

```typescript
// correct
import { WidgetApiService } from '@myorg/data';

// wrong — deep libs path
import { WidgetApiService } from '../../../../libs/data/widget/widget-api.service';

// wrong — raw HttpClient
private http = inject(HttpClient);
```

New or changed API methods, routes, DTO casing or response mapping follow rule `client-data-api-service`. Effects consume the shape that service declares; do not normalize payloads in effects.

## Failure handling

Every effect that can fail must have a `catchError` branch that dispatches a failure action. Never swallow errors silently.

- Failure action name: rule `client-ngrx-actions` (failure action suffix) decides `Error` or `Failure`. Preserve existing action contracts.
- Keep `catchError` on the inner API call, including async exports, so the effect survives a failure.
- When the established failure contract exposes a server-provided reason, pass it through; do not replace it unconditionally with a generic message.

For a hard navigation error (e.g. resource not found), navigate first, then dispatch:

```typescript
catchError(() => {
  this.router.navigate(['/not-found']);
  return of(WidgetActions.loadWidgetError());
})
```

When an effect calls `Router.navigate` or `Router.navigateByUrl`, build the path per skill `client-angular-route`: Router paths are relative to the app's base href.

## Operator selection

| Use case | Operator |
|----------|----------|
| Data fetch, navigation, read | `switchMap` — cancels in-flight on new trigger |
| Sequential writes/mutations | `concatMap` — queues, preserves order |
| Parallel independent calls | `mergeMap` |
| Store reads alongside action | `withLatestFrom` |

## Mutation writes

One `ofType` per mutation effect. Do not listen to two write actions and branch with `'request' in action` or a discriminated context union.

POST the existing request DTO from the API-model library (rule `client-models`), or assemble UI-shaped action props into that DTO. Do not wrap the DTO in an envelope such as `{ id, request }`. Key any in-flight `Set` on a field the DTO already has.

For chained loads, optimistic writes, target or scope identity, request acceptance or rollback, pending records or in-flight counters, read `{CURSOR}/skills/client-ngrx-feature-slice/async-workflows.md`.

## Side-effect-only effects

Effects that only produce side effects (navigation, toast notifications, logging) must set `{ dispatch: false }`.

```typescript
navigateToNotFound$: Observable<void> = createEffect(
  () =>
    this.actions$.pipe(
      ofType(SomeActions.RESOURCE_NOT_FOUND),
      tap(() => this.router.navigate(['/not-found']))
    ),
  { dispatch: false }
);
```

## Toast notifications

Raise toasts through the codebase's existing notification action or service. Do not introduce an app-wide notification factory; feature-local helpers are fine.

When the toast renders through ngx-toastr and the message passes through an HTML formatter, hardcode `enableHtml: true` rather than adding a parameter for it; with `false`, ngx-toastr shows the formatter's tags as literal text.
